From 1e681deb6ed281d30e3dccb54e9f2a764812a8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 20:05:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 251/638] ozone: expose AROS EGL native surfaces [chromium]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-5-gpu-bridge

AI_STATUS: build-validated, runtime-pending

ROOT_CAUSE: The AROS SurfaceFactoryOzone advertised no GL implementation, so Chromium's Ozone GL initializer hit its fail-closed path and unattended recovery removed Chrome_InProcGpuThread, leaving a live browser with a stale compositor surface.

FIX_REASON: Advertise EGL/GLES2, resolve entry points through the linked AROS egl.library, map each AcceleratedWidget back to its real Intuition Window, and create native EGL window and pbuffer surfaces so Chromium enters AROS's existing HIDD/Gallium renderer ladder.

SCOPE: ui/ozone/platform/aros only. Renderer policy remains owned by AROS EGL/Gallium; this does not claim VirGL, Venus, llvmpipe, or hardware acceleration until runtime GL identity proves the selected backend.

HOSTED_NATIVE: shared implementation; focused compilation uses the native x86_64-smp AROS sysroot. Hosted and native runtime validation remain pending.

VALIDATION: bundled clang-format; git diff --cached --check; //ui/ozone/platform/aros:aros cross-build passed. Full chrome link is running under the relay-owned out/aros-windowed scope.

RISK: Medium. The current in-process GPU model shares the ArosWindowManager; a future out-of-process GPU model will require explicit native-window transport.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
